  "behavior": [
    "Replace the public lossy/string-join facade and native raw filepath implementation with one forbidunsafe owning kernel, reached through thin original-owner entry adapters.",
    "Route .Internal(file.path(component_list,fsep)) through its own two-argument handler; public dots/named-fsep construction remains a separate input adapter to that same kernel.",
    "Preserve empty components, NULL/zero-length propagation, recycling and literal missing values. Perform original-order native coercion and validate its character result.",
    "Reject every byte-tagged path component with the exact GNU error; validate separators after the empty-input-list return and retain raw fsep bytes, even when a Latin1 separator produces invalid UTF8-tagged data as GNU does.",
    "Reuse original-heap immutable character translation and prepublication tags. Admit exact translated bytes, row descriptor storage and actual copy-pass concatenation; no output growth beyond its admission when providers change later selections.",
    "Keep selected original components/separator alive after argument detachment and collection; release their roots after output, preserve deliberate callback panic payloads, and deny publication after original runtime revocation.",
    "Remove obsolete raw filepath translation/mkCharCE stubs; retain the eval helper still required by shared native coercion."
  ],
